<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg micro-ocellus wavelength of Drosophila guttifera at 2.12 µm — MorphoEval overall 85.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the periodic Dv sweep (Pearson r = 0.992, RMSE = 0.208 µm, focal centroid 1.983 µm against the 2.12 µm linear calibration). The new zero-flux control selects 1.767 µm. Saturated guttifera peaks are spaced 1.332 µm apart (97 peaks, CV = 0.255, KS = 0.801 against a normal centered on 2.12 µm), so saturation shortens the spacing further; that gap is reported rather than fitted away. The wing-membrane mask counts 18 dark spots against Werner's 16; the pass-1 global threshold had counted 28. Grimshawi coherency remains 0.480 against guttifera 0.010. Heteroneura linear wavelength remains 2.048 µm. Overall 85.0/100 (faithfulness 84.3, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_guttifera_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 479439 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 9e62649b8e7299a09073eacf2e1f3badfaaa2a43786da966ef6bdaee8e4c8305 (sha256 9e62649b8e7299a09073eacf2e1f3badfaaa2a43786da966ef6bdaee8e4c8305), spec_fingerprint c4a6d950a832bc4358255a26def4f385a34b6882ca4a5713ae484c2d3f07773c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c4a6d950a832bc4358255a26def4f385a34b6882ca4a5713ae484c2d3f07773c; artifact_sha256: 9e62649b8e7299a09073eacf2e1f3badfaaa2a43786da966ef6bdaee8e4c8305. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Werner et al. 2010: Wingless at vein intersections and campaniform sensilla induces the yellow wing spots. | Koseki, Tanaka & Koshikawa 2021: wingless expression inside campaniform sensilla. | Turing 1952 marginal wavenumber and Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics.; reconstructed_in_script: Focal parameters a=0.10, b=0.90, Du=0.016, Dv=1.25, scaled so λ(k_max)=2.12 µm. | Periodic spectral centroid on a fixed band, equal-diffusion ablation, reflecting-boundary control, and saturated peak spacing. | Wing-membrane mask: foreground outside the dilated reddish body. | Grimshawi anisotropy 3.15 and heteroneura activator 0.24 at geological age 0 Ma.; transfer_boundary: 2.12 µm is the campaign detail tier. Werner et al. 2010 do not report that length. | The adult photograph cannot resolve 2.12 µm. Its role is the organism, not a micrograph of the grain.; does_not_claim: That the saturated spacing equals 2.12 µm. It is 1.33 µm. | That the zero-flux wavelength equals the periodic calibration. It is 1.77 µm. | That 18 segmented spots are the named 16. Both wings are in the frame. | That Spieth 1981 measured a wing wavelength. It is cited for the heteroneura chronospecies, and the head-shape paper is not a wavelength source. | A second assessor. R4 is still open.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Independent second assessor. Pass 2 is still scored by the builder alone.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'The saturated spacing (1.33 µm) and the zero-flux centroid (1.77 µm) both sit short of 2.12 µm. A weakly nonlinear amplitude expansion, or a fit of Du and Dv to a real micrograph, would be the next measurement. No such micrograph is in this slot.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg micro-ocellus wavelength of Drosophila guttifera at 2.12 µm — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dv still moves the centroid with the analytical curve (r = 0.992) while staying short of the 1:1 line. Anisotropy moves coherency from 0.010 to 0.480. Equal diffusion decays (ratio 0.228). Switching to zero-flux moves the centroid from 1.983 µm to 1.767 µm, so the boundary condition is not inert." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

